import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — derive-DSL root ops: closing the measured sqrt/rsqrt refusal","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/derive-root-ops.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/derive-root-ops.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/derive-root-ops.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-derive-dsl-root-ops-closing-the-measured-sqrt-rsqrt-refusal" tabindex="-1">Retro — derive-DSL root ops: closing the measured <code>sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code> refusal <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-derive-dsl-root-ops-closing-the-measured-sqrt-rsqrt-refusal" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — derive-DSL root ops: closing the measured sqrt/rsqrt refusal”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-10-17. <strong>Scope</strong>: <code>mlopt_core/laws/cond.py</code> (the <code>dspec</code> expression bank), <code>mlopt_discovery/dspec_synth.py</code> (the synthesizer&#39;s search bank), <code>lab/probes/weightspace_fold_probe.py</code>, <code>tests/test_cond_laws.py</code>, <code>tests/test_discovery_dspec_synth.py</code>.</p><p><strong>Depends on</strong>: <code>project/retros/weightspace-fold.md</code> (the measured gate-by-gate refusal this closes one named blocker of), plan 0025 §D3 (the weight-space family — derive-or-refuse).</p><h2 id="what-the-refusal-measured-and-what-changed" tabindex="-1">What the refusal measured, and what changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-refusal-measured-and-what-changed" aria-label="Permalink to “What the refusal measured, and what changed”">​</a></h2><p>The weight-space lane measured the conv+BN fold <code>W&#39; = W·g/√(var+eps)</code>, <code>b&#39; = (b−μ)·g/√(var+eps) + β</code> as <em>structurally derivable but inexpressible</em>: the pre-scaled tier fit (<code>W&#39; = mul(W, scale)</code>; <code>b&#39;</code> at depth 3), so the missing piece was exactly <code>scale = γ·rsqrt(σ²+ε)</code> — and the DSL had no root op (gate 3: <code>dsl_has_sqrt</code>/<code>dsl_has_rsqrt</code> were <code>False</code>; float <code>pow</code> declines). This round adds the measured ops, nothing more:</p><ul><li><strong><code>mlopt_core.laws.cond</code></strong> — <code>_DUNOPS</code> gains <code>&quot;sqrt&quot;: math.sqrt</code> and <code>&quot;rsqrt&quot;: λa. 1/√a</code>. Both are float-valued and strict: <code>math.sqrt</code> raises <code>ValueError</code> on a negative operand, <code>rsqrt</code>&#39;s reciprocal turns a zero operand into <code>ZeroDivisionError</code> — both land in the <code>_unop</code> handler&#39;s <code>(ArithmeticError, TypeError, ValueError)</code> decline set, so the strictness contract (decline, never a fabricated complex or <code>inf</code>) needs no bespoke handler. Grammar doc updated (<code>(&quot;sqrt&quot;|&quot;rsqrt&quot;, e)</code>); both round-trip through <code>derive_to_data</code>/<code>derive_from_data</code> like every other op.</li><li><strong><code>mlopt_discovery.dspec_synth</code></strong> — the <em>search</em> bank widens to match: <code>UNOPS</code> gains <code>sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code>, <code>BINOPS</code> gains <code>fdiv</code> (the true division the refusal formula spelled literally — <code>γ/√(σ²+ε)</code>. <code>fdiv</code> is load-bearing, not decorative: <code>g·rsqrt(·)</code> differs from <code>g/√(·)</code> in the last ulp, so only the <code>fdiv</code>+<code>sqrt</code> spelling can reproduce a <code>/</code>-spelled hook <em>exactly</em> under the synth&#39;s signature-equality gate). <code>_vbin</code>/<code>_vun</code> already route through <code>_DBINOPS</code>/<code>_DUNOPS</code>, so no per-op machinery was needed — the ops are data, per &quot;laws are data&quot;.</li></ul><p><code>pow</code> stays int-only (a float exponent would smuggle a root the strictness contract can&#39;t bound — the probe&#39;s <code>pow_float_exp_declines</code> still measures <code>True</code>).</p><h2 id="the-measured-delta-probe-re-run-fp64" tabindex="-1">The measured delta (probe re-run, fp64) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-measured-delta-probe-re-run-fp64" aria-label="Permalink to “The measured delta (probe re-run, fp64)”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>gate</th><th>before</th><th>after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3 · DSL spellable</td><td><code>dsl_has_sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code> = False</td><td><strong>True/True</strong>; <code>rsqrt_scale_ok</code> — <code>mul(γ, rsqrt(add(var, eps)))</code> evaluates through <code>eval_derive</code></td></tr><tr><td>2c · scale fit <em>(new gate)</em></td><td>—</td><td>depth 2: <strong>no-fit</strong> (17,204 candidates, honest); depth 3: <strong>MINTED</strong> <code>fdiv(float(float(γ)), sqrt(add(ε, var)))</code> — <code>γ/√(ε+σ²)</code>, exact on all 6 measured channels; sweep truncated at the 60 s budget after 133.9 M pairs but the mint is an exact reproduction</td></tr><tr><td>2 · raw fold</td><td><code>W&#39;</code>/<code>b&#39;</code> = None (depth 2–3)</td><td>still <strong>None</strong> — the residual moved: the full fold <code>fdiv(mul(W,γ), sqrt(add(var,ε)))</code> sits at depth ≥ 4 over the 7-attr bank, and the streamed level-3 product no longer terminates in budget. Now an <em>enumeration-depth</em> limit, not an op gap</td></tr><tr><td>4 · value domain</td><td><code>Const.value</code> is <code>int | float</code>; tensor sample raises <code>TypeError</code></td><td><strong>unchanged</strong> — still the dominant blocker</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="what-this-does-and-does-not-buy" tabindex="-1">What this does and does not buy <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-does-and-does-not-buy" aria-label="Permalink to “What this does and does not buy”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Closed</strong>: refusal reason 1 of the weight-space retro (&quot;the DSL has no square root&quot;) — both as spellability (<code>eval_derive</code> computes the scale) and as <em>discoverability</em> (the synthesizer mints the scale expr from measured bindings).</li><li><strong>Open, named</strong>: (a) the derive value domain is still <code>int | float</code> — a per-channel <em>tensor</em> <code>scale</code> cannot be a derived value (gate 4 unchanged); this is the real gate on the conv+BN fold and is an architecture question (<code>bound</code> carries terms, not tensor values; derived attrs must stay JSON-safe; <code>Const.value</code> is typed scalar) — not a one-line op. (b) Enumeration depth: the complete fold expr is depth 4 over a 7-attr bank; the streamed synthesizer found the scale subexpr but the full-expr sweep is budget-bound. (c) Content, not capability: no law LHS names <code>batch_norm</code> (probe gate 5) and <code>batch_norm</code> is unpriced in <code>_OP_FLOPS</code> (gate 6).</li><li>Also fixed en passant: the probe&#39;s <code>_load_audit</code> resolved <code>dspec_audit.py</code> relative to <code>lab/probes/</code> (stale <code>tools/</code>-era path); it now resolves <code>lab/audit/dspec_audit.py</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="gates" tabindex="-1">Gates <a class="header-anchor" href="#gates" aria-label="Permalink to “Gates”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>pytest tests/test_cond_laws.py tests/test_discovery_dspec_synth.py tests/test_discovery_vocab.py tests/test_derive_laws.py tests/test_law_serialize.py</code> — <strong>214 passed</strong> (incl. new <code>TestDeriveRootOps</code> ×4 and <code>TestRootOps</code> ×3: eval, decline semantics — negative/zero/non-numeric — JSON round-trip, bank membership, and two measured mints: <code>rsqrt(add(var,eps))</code> and <code>fdiv</code>/<code>sqrt</code> fits verified through <code>eval_derive</code> on every bound).</li><li><code>pytest tests/test_laws_structure.py tests/test_property_laws.py tests/test_rules.py tests/test_laws_rewrite_edges.py</code> — 51 passed (the widened bank disturbs no structural pin; <code>pow</code> still refuses).</li><li><code>ruff check</code> / <code>ruff format --check</code> on the touched shipped files — clean (the two <code>tests/</code> files carry the repo&#39;s documented pre-existing format drift; the additions themselves are clean).</li><li><code>ty check</code> — 0 errors. <code>lint-imports</code> — 4 contracts kept (<code>math</code> is stdlib; core stays torch-free).</li><li><code>vulture</code> — one finding, <strong>pre-existing and not mine</strong>: <code>tests/test_form_propose.py:142</code> (an <code>if False else</code> ternary, committed in <code>fb34e18</code> — the state-reindex agent&#39;s file, left for them).</li></ul>`,13)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};